## Code knowledge graph (graphy)

This repository has a pre-built code knowledge graph in `.graphy/`. For
architecture and impact questions, query the graph instead of scanning files:

- `graphy query "<question>"` — relevant entities + relationships for a
  natural-language question (works offline without an API key)
- `graphy path <a> <b>` — how two entities connect
- `graphy explain <entity>` — location, signature, community, all edges
- `graphy report` — stats, god nodes, subsystem communities, rationale

The graph also holds `rationale` nodes — WHY:/DECISION:/HACK: comments and
architecture decision records — joined to the code they justify by `explains`
edges. Ask "why does X work this way?" before changing unfamiliar code.

After editing code, run `graphy update` (incremental, sub-second) to keep the
graph fresh. `graphy mcp` serves these as MCP stdio tools.
